# Session Day vs Name

Do **not** invent a second date. Do **not** add a new backend column. Do **not** encode Day inside `title`. Do **not** make Day a Monday–Sunday weekday. Sessions stay **dated workouts**; calendar date is already first-class.

Source of truth: `architecture.md` §5.1 Workout (`date`, `dayLabel`, `title`, optional `block_label` / `week_label`). This rule **overrides** `design.md` §16.3 “New session dialog is name + optional block/week” and `knowledge.md` surfaces that treat Name as the only identity besides Block/Week. Patch those lines in the **implementation** PR.

This checkout has **no** `SessionCreateForm`. Create lives in `NewSessionDialog`. There is **no** ComboBox component; Name is a freeform `<input>` defaulting to `"Session"`. `LabelCombo` is a skinny native `<select>` used for Block/Week only.

---

## Grill (locked answers — do not re-litigate)

| Challenge | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- |
| Is Day the calendar date, weekday, or a training-slot label? | **Training-slot label** (Day 1–Day 7 / D1–D7), independent of `date`. Architecture already has `dayLabel` (`src/types.ts`: `e.g. "D1"`). Date is the calendar field. Weekday would invent required Mon–Sun week containers (`AGENTS.md` / architecture forbid that). Insights `weekday_matrix` already buckets by **calendar weekday from `date`** — do not retarget it at `dayLabel`. |
| Why not use the date as the day? | Date is already chosen (calendar hover / date input). Coaches reuse **Day 1** across weeks on different dates. Using ISO date as `dayLabel` (today’s create/copy fallback) duplicates Date and makes copy-week alignment by slot impossible. |
| Why a dropdown vs the existing Name combobox? | **There is no Name combobox.** Name is a text input whose default is `"Session"`; users type `"day 1"` into the title because that is the only free field. Day is a small closed-ish vocabulary; Name is a freeform session title (Squat, Meet, Upper). Merging them is the bug. |
| Collision with Week copy **D1**? | Copy-to “destination Calendar day = **D1**” means **earliest source date** (`copyClipboard.ts` `dateOffsetDays`). That is **not** `workout.dayLabel`. Do not reuse copy-grain “D1” copy in the Day control. Display Day as **Day 1**, not `D1`, so the two languages do not collide. Store canonical `"1"`…`"7"`. |
| Persistence: per athlete vs global? | **Athlete-scoped**, same pattern as `al_recent_block:{athleteId}`. Coach switching athletes must not leak another athlete’s Day 3 / “Squat”. |
| Unlabeled sessions? | Allowed. `dayLabel` is NOT NULL, so create-without-Day keeps the existing ISO-date fallback. UI treats ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (and empty) as **unlabeled** — do not render “Day 2026-09-04”. |
| Copy-week? | `clone_session_prescription` currently sets `dayLabel=new_date` (destroys the slot). **Preserve** source `dayLabel` when it is a real slot (not ISO). If source is unlabeled (ISO/empty), keep dest-date fallback. Titles already copy. Do not ask for Day on paste. |
| Google Sheets? | Publish already has columns Date, **Day** (`dayLabel`), Title (`integrations.py` Workouts tab). No schema change. Filling real Day 1 makes Day ≠ Date. One-way publish only. |
| New backend column / title prefix? | **No.** `dayLabel` already exists on create/update (`CreateSessionRequest.dayLabel`, `apiService.createSession`). Wire it. Do not prefix `"Day 1 · "` into `title`. Do not migrate historical ISO `dayLabel` rows. |

