## Spec

### Meaning

- **Date** — when the workout happens. Unchanged.
- **Day** — training-slot label inside a block/week template (`dayLabel`). Independent of weekday and of Name.
- **Name** — session title (`title`). Not “Day 1”.
- **Week / Block** — optional grouping labels. Unchanged.

### Canonical Day values

- Presets always listed: **Day 1 … Day 7**.
- Store `"1"` … `"7"`. Aliases `D1`, `d1`, `Day1`, `Day 1` normalize to `"1"` (same idea as `formatPlanLabel` stripping `Week`/`Block`).
- Display: extend `formatPlanLabel` with kind `'Day'` → `"Day 1"`. Never show raw `D1` in the session header.
- Custom slots allowed (type in the ComboBox): `"8"`, `"AM"`, `"Meet"`. Display `Day {stripped}` when it is a numeric/Day-prefixed token; otherwise show the custom string (do not force `"Day Meet"` if that reads worse — custom non-numeric displays as typed).
- Unlabeled: `dayLabel` empty or matching `ISO_DATE` (`/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/`). `formatPlanLabel('Day', iso)` returns **null**.

### ComboBox (new, reuse for Day and Name)

There is no ComboBox in tree. Add a small one (new file or next to `LabelCombo.tsx`). **Do not** use native `<select>` for Day or Name.

- Text input + visible listbox (`role="listbox"` / `role="option"`). Filter as you type. ArrowUp/Down highlight; Enter picks; click picks; Escape does not fight `CenteredDialog` (let the dialog keep Escape-to-close when the list is closed).
- Easy pick: last value already in the input; one click/arrow to change.
- Day options = presets 1–7 ∪ unique non-ISO `dayLabel`s from the plan (normalized).
- Name options = **`uniquePlanTitles(microcycles)`**: unique trimmed `workout.title`, exclude `""` and `"Session"`.
- Custom / unknown value stays valid (Name is always freeform; Day allows custom).
- Block/Week may stay `LabelCombo` this pass.

### New session (`NewSessionDialog`)

Layout: Date (if `allowDateEdit`) → **Day** ComboBox → **Name** ComboBox → Block / Week.

Prefill when the dialog opens (athlete id = linked athlete for coach, else current user — same as `setRecentBlock`):

| Field | Source |
| :--- | :--- |
| Day | `al_recent_day:{athleteId}` |
| Name | `al_recent_name:{athleteId}` — **never** the literal `"Session"` |
| Block | existing `getRecentBlock` (today stored, not prefilled — **prefill it**) |
| Week | add `al_recent_week:{athleteId}` on the same helper pattern |

- Name placeholder if no last name: `Name` or `Squat, Meet…` — input value `""`, not `"Session"`. Create with empty Name: require a name (`setError`) rather than silently saving `"Session"`.
- Day may stay empty (unlabeled). Do not infer Day from the calendar weekday of `date`.
- On successful create: `setRecentDay` / `setRecentName` / `setRecentBlock` / `setRecentWeek` when those fields are non-empty. Send `dayLabel` only when Day is labeled; omit so backend keeps ISO fallback when unlabeled.
- Keep `data-testid="new-session-title"` on the Name input. Add `new-session-day`.

### Edit (`EditSessionDialog`) + header

- Same Day + Name ComboBoxes. Day initial = unlabeled if ISO, else stored slot.
- Save sends `title` and `dayLabel` (ISO date when Day cleared, to keep NOT NULL unlabeled sentinel).
- Header (`App.tsx` `session-name` / `session-labels`): **Name (`title`)** then **Day n** (if labeled) then Week n then Block n. Do not put Day in `session-name`. Unlabeled Day omitted (keep `No block/week` only when both week and block empty; Day absence is not that message).
- Calendar/Sessions cards may keep showing **title** only this pass.

### Copy / Sheets / Telegram

- Copy grain language unchanged (dest click = date D1).
- `clone_session_prescription`: `dayLabel = source.dayLabel` unless unlabeled (ISO/empty) → then `new_date`.
- Sheets: no change besides real values in Day.
- Telegram: already shows `dayLabel`; formatting Day 1 is optional/out of scope.

### Pref keys (`src/storage/uiPrefs.ts`)

LocalStorage UI prefs only (not IndexedDB, not sync):

- `al_recent_block` (exists)
- `al_recent_week`
- `al_recent_day`
- `al_recent_name`

Helpers mirror `getRecentBlock` / `setRecentBlock` (`:athleteId` suffix). Coach uses the **plan athlete** id, not the coach user id.

### Backend

- **No new column.** Create/PATCH already accept `dayLabel`.
- One behavior fix: copy clone preserves labeled `dayLabel` (above).
- Do not parse Day from `title`.
- Do not auto-seed Day 1 on empty plans.

